<% layout("layouts/boilerplate") %>
<div class="content">
  <h1>Welcome to Gram Bharti College Ramgarh</h1>
  <img src="/images/campus.webp" alt="College Image" class="college-img" />
  <p class="college-desc">
    Gram Bharti College, Ramgarh, Kaimur (Bihar), 821110, a constituent college
    of Veer Kunwar Singh University and a UGC-registered institution, offers a
    range of undergraduate programmes designed to support students in building
    strong academic and professional foundations.
    <br />
    The college offers four-year undergraduate programmes in Bachelor of Arts
    (B.A.), Bachelor of Science (B.Sc.), and Bachelor of Commerce (B.Com.) along
    with three-year professional programmes in Bachelor of Computer Applications
    (BCA), and Bachelor of Business Administrationg (BBA) both approved by
    AICTE.
  </p>

  <section class="recognition-section" id="recognition-section">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Recognition & Approvals</h2>
      <p>
        Verify the university recognition and programme approval through the
        respective official regulatory authorities.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="recognition-content">
      <h3>UGC Recognition</h3>
      <p>
        Verify the recognition of Veer Kunwar Singh University through the
        official UGC website.
      </p>

      <a
        href="https://www.ugc.gov.in/universitydetails/university?type=MuOh4z0uqRaY2k8Ag10I0g=="
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Verify University Recognition
        <span><i class="fa-solid fa-square-arrow-up-right"></i></span>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="recognition-content">
      <h3>AICTE Approval</h3>
      <p>
        Verify the approval status of the BCA programme through the official
        AICTE portal.
      </p>

      <a
        href="https://facilities.aicte-india.org/dashboard/pages/angulardashboard.php#!/approved"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
      >
        Verify AICTE Approval
        <span><i class="fa-solid fa-square-arrow-up-right"></i></span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
  <div class="map-embed" id="college-map">
    <iframe
      src="https://www.google.com/maps/embed?pb=!1m18!1m12!1m3!1d3607.1053406710366!2d83.6585722743806!3d25.3006646275039!2m3!1f0!2f0!3f0!3m2!1i1024!2i768!4f13.1!3m3!1m2!1s0x398de374c0000001%3A0xf4efeeaf7bf7a027!2sGram%20Bharti%20College%20Ramgarh!5e0!3m2!1sen!2sin!4v1790609381525!5m2!1sen!2sin"
      title="Map showing Gram Bharti College"
      allowfullscreen
      loading="lazy"
      referrerpolicy="strict-origin-when-cross-origin"
    ></iframe>
  </div>
  <button id="locate-btn" type="button">Find distance to college</button>
  <p id="distance-result"></p>

  <section class="home-faq" aria-labelledby="home-faq-title">
    <div class="home-faq-heading">
      <p class="home-faq-eyebrow">Student information</p>
      <h2 id="home-faq-title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <p>Quick answers about Gram Bharti College and BCA student resources.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="home-faq-list">
      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>Where is Gram Bharti College located?</summary>
        <p>
          The college is in Ramgarh, Kaimur, Bihar, 821110.
          <a href="#college-map">View the college map</a> for directions.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>Which undergraduate programmes does the college offer?</summary>
        <p>
          The college offers four-year B.A., B.Sc. and B.Com. programmes, along
          with three-year BCA and BBA programmes.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>Which university is the college affiliated with?</summary>
        <p>
          Gram Bharti College is a constituent college of Veer Kunwar Singh
          University. You can <a href="#recognition-section">view the recognition and approval links</a>
          on this page.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>Where can I find BCA question papers?</summary>
        <p>
          Semester 1 papers are listed for 2024–2027 and 2025–2028 batches;
          Semester 2 papers are listed for 2025–2028. <a href="/pyq/bca">Browse papers and solutions by semester.</a>
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>How long is the BCA programme?</summary>
        <p>
          BCA is a three-year undergraduate programme. <a href="/programme/bca">See BCA programme resources.</a>
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>Where can I get the BCA syllabus and assignment front pages?</summary>
        <p>
          View or download the <a href="/programme/bca#syllabus">BCA syllabus PDF</a> and the
          <a href="/programme/bca#assignment-front-page">combined assignment front-page PDF</a>.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>What uniform is listed for BCA students?</summary>
        <p>
          The listed outfits are black pants, white shirt, black shoes and white socks for boys;
          black salwar, white suit and black dupatta for girls. The listed boys' outfit is also an option.
          <a href="/programme/bca#uniform">View uniform details.</a>
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="home-faq-item">
        <summary>What are the BCA fees?</summary>
        <p>
          For the 2025–2028 batch, estimated semester fees total ₹68,500–₹80,500. Including exams at
          ₹1,000 per semester, the estimate is ₹74,500–₹86,500 if that rate remains unchanged.
          These are not official current rates; confirm with the BCA HOD. <a href="/programme/bca#fees">See the fee breakdown.</a>
        </p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>
<script src="/js/location.js"></script>
